From c596013f19dc86afc438e678f48eb51ae1cbfc04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:41:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] state: confirm structural corruption once before
 latching state.db for the process
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

One unconfirmed "database disk image is malformed" (2026-11-04 00:01Z, inside a
compression split on hermes-hub) set the process-wide storage latch; every write
(worker receipts, transcripts) was then refused for an hour until a restart, on a
file that later passed quick_check on all 36 tables + 8 FTS tables.

Writer (_execute_write): a structural corrupt error raised by BEGIN or the callback,
with the rollback confirmed (conn.in_transaction is False) and the connection's
unpinned page cache released (PRAGMA shrink_memory), is replayed once on the same
connection. A recurrence latches as before. Never replayed: COMMIT (settlement
unknown — a durable receipt would apply twice), anything after commit, an
unconfirmed rollback, a failed cache release. FTS-scoped corruption keeps its
fail-open path, checked first, unchanged.
Reader (_read_retrying_ioerr): one replay of a structural error before latching.
Latch reason / ERROR line now carry sqlite=<name>(<code>), op=<callback qualname>,
stage=<begin|callback|commit|committed> and the replay outcome; a replay that
succeeds logs "did not recur ... NOT latched (unconfirmed corruption)".

Five whys (selfheal gateway-d7a592a91c, proposal.md):
Problem: 2026-11-03 16:26-17:01 PT every state.db write on hermes-hub refused with
  StateDbCorruptError (gateway.log.3:6085-6134); 2 worker runs crashed.
Why 1: _raise_if_db_corrupt(storage=True) refuses every write once the
  process-wide flag is set (hermes_state.py _raise_if_db_corrupt).
Why 2: the flag was set by one error at 00:01:06Z; mark_storage_corrupt keeps the
  first error and never re-checks (hermes_state_health.py mark_storage_corrupt).
Why 3: any bare SQLITE_CORRUPT without FTS provenance counted as structural with
  no confirmation (is_structural_corruption_error -> _halt_db_corrupt).
Why 4: the file was not damaged: read-only quick_check passed on every table; 20,900+
  messages saved after the restart (hypothesis on mechanism: one-off misread /
  since-replaced page; 00:01 logs rotated).
Root (happened): design assumed "corrupt once, corrupt forever" with no confirmation
  step and restart as the only exit.
Root (not caught): test_storage_health_latch.py only injected persistent damage; no
  test injected a one-shot error, and the latch reason kept only the message text.
Recurrence: first false positive since the latch landed (bd945ec3845, #120274).
Countermeasures:
- symptom/root: confirm-by-replay above — proof: tests/hermes_state/
  test_storage_corruption_confirmation.py (one-shot callback/BEGIN/read/receipt/
  split RED on base -> GREEN).
- safety: persistent fault, real damaged B-tree page, unconfirmed rollback, COMMIT
  fault, durable-commit-then-error (exactly-once receipt), FTS-scoped fault +
  refused detach stay fail-closed / on their path — proof: same file; a blind-retry
  mutant fails 3 of them, an FTS-reroute mutant fails 2.
- detection: reason carries code/op/stage/replay outcome; "did not recur" WARNING.
- deferred (owner t_01a1a5a82366d7e6): scoped fresh read-only quick_check
  confirmation per that card's acceptance; coach rule on "unconfirmed corruption".
